<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Histiaea</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hestiaea, Oreus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Histiaea was an ancient Greek city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Euboea</a>, controlling the strait facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>. After it revolted against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> in 446 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pericles">Pericles</a> expelled its inhabitants and replaced them with Athenian settlers, and the town became known as Oreus. Later it changed hands among Athens, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> and joined the Euboean League.</p></div>
